    <element identifier="id-3db5d26be8ff5636bce7ce69f352db3c" xsi:type="Node">
      <name>Static Web App</name>
      <documentation>Azure Static Web App (Free tier) hosting the public/ frontend and its integrated Functions API (api/).</documentation>
      <properties>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-1">
          <value>Free</value>
        </property>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-2">
          <value>platform</value>
        </property>
      </properties>
    </element>
    <element identifier="id-d447595fb73a5ff29894857ab28f8ffe" xsi:type="Node">
      <name>Azure SQL Server</name>
      <documentation>Logical SQL server for the sample app's database.</documentation>
      <properties>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-2">
          <value>platform</value>
        </property>
      </properties>
    </element>
    <element identifier="id-f0ecd6fb3b8b5bb69f24b39169314ce4" xsi:type="Artifact">
      <name>appdb</name>
      <documentation>Free-tier serverless Azure SQL database (GP_S_Gen5). Holds dbo.DemoItems, created and seeded by the API on first request.</documentation>
      <properties>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-1">
          <value>GP_S_Gen5 (free limit, auto-pause)</value>
        </property>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-2">
          <value>platform</value>
        </property>
      </properties>
    </element>
    <element identifier="id-1ee4629338065d2fafc10f0f4fd6becc" xsi:type="Artifact">
      <name>Database Config</name>
      <documentation>Microsoft.Web/staticSites/config "appsettings" (main.bicep staticSiteAppSettings) — SQL_SERVER, SQL_DATABASE, SQL_USER, SQL_PASSWORD read by the Items API at runtime.</documentation>
      <properties>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-2">
          <value>platform</value>
        </property>
      </properties>
    </element>
    <element identifier="id-5deb57760c7b5ff782805afdf0a52709" xsi:type="CommunicationNetwork">
      <name>No-VNet Azure Network</name>
      <documentation>Neither side has VNet integration or Private Link: the Static Web App (Visitor HTTPS ingress via the Web App Interface, and egress to SQL — no VNet option on Free tier) and the SQL Server's public endpoint (publicNetworkAccess: Enabled) share this unisolated network plane. Not the open internet: SQL access is additionally gated by the AllowAzureServices firewall rule, which admits any Azure tenant's services, not arbitrary internet hosts.</documentation>
      <properties>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-3">
          <value>Enabled</value>
        </property>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-4">
          <value>AllowAzureServices (0.0.0.0-0.0.0.0)</value>
        </property>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-5">
          <value>1.2</value>
        </property>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-2">
          <value>platform</value>
        </property>
      </properties>
    </element>
    <element identifier="id-b9118a54ded651d7b8872524243f8f51" xsi:type="ApplicationComponent">
      <name>Items API</name>
      <documentation>TypeScript Azure Functions API (api/src/functions/items.ts). The page calls /api/items; on first request it creates dbo.DemoItems and inserts three sample rows if the table is empty.</documentation>
      <properties>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-2">
          <value>platform</value>
        </property>
      </properties>
    </element>
    <element identifier="id-859316e8097157ce823a81f45e5be19b" xsi:type="ApplicationComponent">
      <name>Frontend</name>
      <documentation>Static browser app (public/index.html, public/app.js). Calls GET /api/items on page load and renders the returned DemoItem rows.</documentation>
      <properties>
        <property propertyDefinitionRef="propid-2">
          <value>platform</value>
        </property>
      </properties>
    </element>
    <element identifier="id-27cc7f943927547f96ea28fdf6f271ed" xsi:type="ApplicationInterface">
      <name>/api/items Interface</name>
      <documentation>HTTP interface exposed by the Items API component for the frontend to call.</documentation>
